WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.544
Hello, welcome to How We Made Your Mother.
大家好，欢迎收听《老爸老妈的浪漫史幕后故事》。

00:00:04.544 --> 00:00:15.975
This is our bonus episode, which we lovingly and faithfully refer to as general questions, general questions.
这是我们的特别番外篇，我们充满爱意且忠实地称它为“常规问题、常规问题”。

00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:18.178
That was pretty good.
那个挺不错的。

00:00:18.178 --> 00:00:21.324
That was actually pretty good.
那个其实真的挺不错。

00:00:21.324 --> 00:00:29.190
We're trying to sync this up and it was one of our more successful efforts.
我们正努力把它俩合拍上，这是我们比较成功的一次尝试。

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:50.060
This is a these are questions about episode seven, the matchmaker and the cockamouse, which if If that is a detail that orients you more into the story than the more enduring story from that episode.
这是一个……这些是关于第七集《红娘》和“蟑螂鼠”的问题，如果这个细节比那一集里更长久的故事更能让你联想到剧情的话。

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:58.579
So we're talking about the matchmaker, we're talking about the cockamouse and we'll hand it over to our beloved producer and friend, Alec Lev, who will fire these questions our way.
所以我们聊的是《红娘》，聊的是“蟑螂鼠”，我们要把它交给我们的挚爱制作人兼朋友阿莱克·莱夫，由他来向我们抛出这些问题。

00:00:58.579 --> 00:00:59.579
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:05.859
I want to start out with a question that I'm piecing together something from dozens of not hundreds of questions.
我想从一个问题开始，我把成百上千个问题中的一些内容拼凑在了一起。

00:01:05.859 --> 00:01:11.459
I think people just like to hear about life on set, like literally on the set.
我想人们只是喜欢听听片场的生活，字面意思上的片场生活。

00:01:11.459 --> 00:01:21.439
They'd love to hear about you know when people when people break and you make people laugh But just anything about where where do you keep your script and and are you eating in the middle of it?
他们很想听听，你知道的，当大家笑场的时候，你们是怎么让大家笑的，或者任何关于你们把剧本藏在哪里的事，以及你们在拍戏间隙会吃东西吗？

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:26.519
Just those little little fun facts that I think people would enjoy hearing Josh.
就这些我觉得大家会乐于听到的小趣事，乔什。

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:31.980
Yeah, well key note address about You know what's it what's life like on a sitcom set?
好的，那么关于“情景喜剧片场的生活是什么样的”的主题演讲来咯？

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.834
I mean we're on stage 22 at the Fox lot in West LA.
我的意思是，我们在西洛杉矶福克斯片场的22号摄影棚。

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:52.459
It's it's a huge like aircraft hangar basically Um, if you look up, there's just, it looks like endless wood and beams and cross, you know, things in the sky and there's lights hanging from and yeah, hugely high ceiling.
它基本上就像一个巨大的飞机机库。

00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:57.780
Um, probably, uh, yeah, not great for your allergies.
如果你抬头看，到处都是无尽的木头、横梁，你知道的，天花板上有各种交叉的东西，灯就挂在上面，而且天花板真的超级高。

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:03.340
Um, but, um, there's like dust from Planet of the Apes and flying around in there.
可能，呃，对你的过敏症不太友好。

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.980
I think Planet of the Apes was out there.
但是，呃，里面到处都是《人猿星球》留下的灰尘在飞舞。

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:05.980
Yeah.
我觉得《人猿星球》就是在那里拍的。

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.460
Some really classic old Hollywood movies were shot on that stage.
是的。

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.460
It was really fun.
一些非常经典的老好莱坞电影就是在那个摄影棚里拍的。

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:17.340
Also, when you're on the Fox, if you drive in the front gate, you see the huge painted Simpsons mural.
真的很酷。

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.939
There's, isn't Darth Vader and Luke Skywalker, there was a thing on there.
还有，如果你从福克斯的前门开车进去，你会看到巨大的辛普森一家手绘壁画。

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:28.340
So you drive on to these lots and you feel like you're in old Hollywood kind of immediately.
还有，那上面不是还有达斯·维达和卢克·天行者吗，以前有个那样的东西。

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.099
It's really- And in the shadow of the die-hard building, also.
所以当你开车进入这些片场时，你会立刻觉得自己身处老好莱坞。

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:32.099
That's right.
真的……而且也笼罩在《虎胆龙威》大楼的阴影之下。

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:35.340
We looked up and saw the die-hard building for nine seasons.
没错。

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:48.539
You know, there's a, there's a candy cart floating around that has like, like any candy you could ever imagine, but it also had a, uh, uh, uh, weren't there piles of scripts that if you needed a script, like the latest revision of the script?
我们抬头就能看到《虎胆龙威》大楼，看了整整九季。

00:02:48.539 --> 00:02:59.900
So I think like when you're on a show, especially if you're on camera, you have to train yourself, you cannot eat all the candy you want because you will look different by the end of the season than you did when you started.
你知道的，那里有个到处移动的糖果车，上面有你能想象到的任何糖果，但它也有一个，呃，呃，呃，难道不是有一堆剧本吗？如果你需要剧本的话，比如最新修订版的剧本？

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.460
It's really true.
所以我觉得当你在出演一部剧时，特别是如果你要在镜头前出镜，你必须克制自己，你不能随心所欲地吃所有糖果，因为到这一季结束时，你的外表会和刚开始时不一样。

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.280
I remember I would, I never liked carrying the whole script.
这绝对是真的。

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.280
I would rip out the three pages, four pages of the scene.
我记得我以前，从来不喜欢把整本剧本随身携带。

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.740
And I would rehearse them most of the time.
我会撕下那场戏的三四页。

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:22.939
I was somewhat off book, sometimes I wasn't, but I would, sometimes if it was just a little, I would just isolate what my lines and I would have them.
然后我会练习它们，大多数时候我差不多能脱稿，有时不能，但有时如果只是一小部分，我就会把我的台词单独拿出来，然后带着它们。

00:03:22.939 --> 00:03:30.860
And then I would either, I'd put them under a prop on the desk, you know, like on a desk or a lot of pages underneath.
然后我会把它们塞在桌子上的某个道具下面，你知道的，比如放在桌上或者一堆纸下面。

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:38.699
I'm sure that a props and set dressing were just finding pages stuffed in couch cushions and behind pillows constantly.
我敢确定，道具组和布景师肯定经常在沙发垫子里和抱枕后面翻出塞进去的剧本页。

00:03:38.699 --> 00:03:41.180
Because you forget that you left them there, right?
因为你会忘记自己把它们落在那儿了，对吧？

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.419
I would have them in my back pocket.
我会把它们塞进后裤兜里。

00:03:42.419 --> 00:03:47.340
Sometimes wardrobe would have to come through and say, oh, your script's poking out, your back pocket.
有时服装组不得不走过来提醒说：“哦，你的剧本露出来啦，在后裤兜里。”

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:59.759
But the other thing that we would do, especially if there was a scene with all five of us, and what's weird is the more successful the show gets, the lazier the actors get.
但我们做的另一件事，特别是如果有我们全部五个人的群戏时——诡异的是，剧越成功，演员就越懒。

00:03:59.759 --> 00:04:15.424
because you get better at doing it, you get better at, you get better at doing it, you get better at, you know your character, I mean, it's so hand in glove, you're just, you know how to play this character, you own the character, they know you own it.
因为你越来越擅长演戏了，你越来越擅长……你越来越擅长表演，你知道你的角色，我的意思是，这简直是不谋而合，你就是，你知道如何扮演这个角色，你对角色驾轻就熟，他们也知道你吃透了这个角色。

00:04:15.424 --> 00:04:21.765
So we had this wonderful script supervisor named Janet Kagan, who was British and sassy and hilarious.
所以我们有一位非常棒的剧本总监叫珍妮特·卡根，她是英国人，性格泼辣又搞笑。

00:04:21.765 --> 00:04:25.246
And she was always right next to Pam behind the monitor.
她总是坐在监视器后面的帕姆旁边。

00:04:25.246 --> 00:04:33.700
And she marks up like where people got lime I'm strong or right or circles takes that Pam says, that's a good take and she'll circle it.
她会标记出大家的台词哪里说得很有力量或很准确，或者把帕姆说“这条不错”的镜头圈起来。

00:04:33.699 --> 00:04:35.139
And it's a whole like code.
那是一套完整的密码。

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:38.980
She's got colored pencils and all sorts of stuff that I never understood.
她有彩色铅笔和各种我从没搞懂的东西。

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.540
But we would often gather around and Janet would run lines with us.
但我们经常聚在一起，让珍妮特陪我们对台词。

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.300
And we would do that right before we shot.
我们会在开拍前就这样做。

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.860
We would just gather around Janet's podium and learn the lines, you know, not always.
我们就会聚在珍妮特的立式台子周围背台词，你知道的，也不是每次都这样。

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.379
Sometimes we would come in and we'd really have them.
有时我们走进片场时就已经把台词背得滚瓜烂熟了。

00:04:54.379 --> 00:04:57.379
But a lot of times you were learning as you went.
但很多时候你都是在边做边学。

00:04:57.379 --> 00:05:05.740
And then the moment she was funny to witness because it would be like, you're acting and you're trying to get out of your workings and seeing it, working through the lines a little bit and Janet would be like eating a bowl of her puffins.
而且当时看她觉得挺逗的，因为你会看到她一边在演戏，一边努力跳脱出自己的表演状态去揣摩，稍微琢磨一下台词，而珍妮特（Janet）就在那一边吃着一碗她的帕芬脆。

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.199
And just be like, what's the mean by breaking up?
然后就来一句：“分手的点在哪里啊？”

00:05:08.199 --> 00:05:09.100
And then just go back to it.
接着又马上投入到状态中。

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.199
You should be doing that.
你真该学学她那样。

00:05:10.199 --> 00:05:21.060
It was also great to hear Janet, this British woman like reading Barney lines, like reading like the kind of gnarliest Barney lines in this thick British accent.
而且听到珍妮特这个英国女人念巴尼的台词也很有意思，就像是用那种浓重的英国腔念着巴尼最离谱的台词。

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.139
It was really funny.
真的太搞笑了。

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:32.300
So yeah, I mean, it was always kind of, you know, I'd walk in and if we were there in the morning you kind of blaze through craft service and maybe grab some oatmeal and a cup of coffee.
所以，对啊，我的意思是，感觉一直都是这样，你知道的，我走进去，如果早上我们就在那儿，你就会顺路去后勤餐饮区（craft service）匆忙拿点燕麦片和一杯咖啡。

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.339
And you ask him craft service like what's for lunch?
然后你问后勤的人：“午饭吃什么？”

00:05:35.339 --> 00:05:36.819
You know, it's just rice.
你知道的，就是米饭。

00:05:36.819 --> 00:05:38.139
Breakfast rice.
早餐饭。

00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:40.579
We did often freak out about how much we love breakfast.
我们确实经常为我们有多爱早餐而大惊小怪。

00:05:40.579 --> 00:05:41.420
Breakfast rice was good.
早餐饭挺不错的。

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.379
I think that was in the later seasons.
我想那是在后面的几季里。

00:05:43.379 --> 00:05:44.300
Yeah, it was.
对，确实是。

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.939
Yeah.
对。

00:05:45.939 --> 00:05:47.980
But you know, it becomes your home away from home.
但你知道的，那成了你的第二个家。

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.220
You know, you have your meals there.
你知道的，你在那儿吃饭。

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.259
You get to know the crew.
你开始认识剧组的工作人员。

00:05:53.259 --> 00:05:55.660
You get to know the crews, spouses and kids.
你开始认识工作人员的配偶和孩子。

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:07.139
And I don't know, I think that people, when they watch how I met your mother, I think I've said this before, they think it's five people, but it's 75 people.
而且我不知道，我觉得人们在看《老爸老妈浪漫史》时——我想我以前也说过这个——他们觉得只有五个人，但其实有75个人。

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:10.459
You know, the set is a buzz with people.
你知道的，片场到处都是人，非常热闹。

00:06:10.459 --> 00:06:19.100
And when in between scenes, people are coming along and they're fussing with your face and they're fussing with your hair and they're giving you a note and they're fussing with your collar.
在两场戏的间隙，大家会围过来，给你整理脸上的妆容，给你弄弄头发，给你提点意见，顺便帮你整理一下衣领。

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:24.100
You know, there's just a very active life going on on set.
你知道的，片场里正进行着非常生动的生活。

00:06:25.779 --> 00:06:26.360
Yeah.
对。

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:26.940
Yeah.
对。

00:06:26.939 --> 00:06:30.740
And it really matters what that energy is of that life, what that kind of ecosystem is.
而这种生活的能量是什么样的，那种生态系统是什么样的，其实非常重要。

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.139
And that's a lot of people bringing that energy.
那是许多人把这种能量带到了片场。

00:06:33.139 --> 00:06:39.980
And we just had an amazing, amazing crew that just had the warmest energy where everybody felt safe to do their best work.
我们拥有一个非常、非常棒的剧组，他们有着最温暖的能量，让每个人都觉得在这里可以安心地发挥出最好的水平。

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:43.579
And it was fantastic, doesn't always happen.
这太棒了，这种事并不总是会发生。

00:06:43.579 --> 00:06:45.019
A couple of things I could point out.
我有几点可以指出来。

00:06:45.019 --> 00:06:53.100
Among the productions from stage 22 on the old 20th Century Fox Lot, Dr. Do Little, 1967.
在老二十世纪福克斯片场第22号摄影棚的作品中，有1967年的《怪医杜立德》。

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.282
Oh, cool.
哦，太酷了。

00:06:54.282 --> 00:06:54.939
Yeah.
对。

00:06:54.939 --> 00:07:11.773
Planet of the Apes 1968 I knew it and nine to five 1980 I forgot about that nine to five so that's a fucking great movie I I did not appreciate that enough at the time that we were like they're shooting dad me Coleman office scenes on there something come on Yeah, come on.
1968年的《人猿星球》，我猜到了，还有1980年的《朝九晚五》，我都忘了还有《朝九晚五》，所以那真是一部他妈的好电影，我当时还没有充分意识到这一点，我们就好像是在那儿拍老爸科尔曼的办公室场景什么的，拜托，得了吧，对，得了吧。

00:07:11.773 --> 00:07:26.818
Yeah, that's fantastic So meals I know as I was only there in the later season to sort of put together what we were talking about in the main episode of this episode talking about this episode of the technology sure and Josh your comfort level.
对，太棒了。所以关于吃饭，我知道——因为我只在后几季才加入，来整理一下我们在本集的主节目里讨论的内容，关于本集的科技，当然还有Josh你当时的舒适度。

00:07:26.818 --> 00:07:37.485
I just remember closing in the seasons eight and nine, the delta, the time between cut and the cell phone coming out to make a call to Scott shorter and shorter and shorter.
我只记得在第八季和第九季的尾声，导演喊“卡”之后，到拿出手机给斯科特打电话之间的时间间隔，变得越来越短，越来越短，越来越短。

00:07:37.485 --> 00:07:39.088
Where was that cell phone?
那手机是从哪儿拿出来的？

00:07:39.088 --> 00:07:41.740
How would you already have it in your hand?
你怎么会已经把它拿在手上了？

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:45.143
Pam is very, very, Pam is the loveliest director of the loveliest human.
帕姆（Pam）是个非常、非常优秀的导演，也是个极好的人。

00:07:45.143 --> 00:07:47.932
She's the kindest person she never got mad at anybody once.
她是那种最善良的人，一次也没有对任何人发过火。

00:07:47.932 --> 00:07:53.794
I never saw her as her voice, but she would have been knowing and have these little passive aggressive things she would say.
我从来没见她大声说过话，但她会心领神会，并说出一些带有这种微小被动攻击性的话。

00:07:53.794 --> 00:07:55.827
And she was always in the right, of course.
当然，而且她总是对的。

00:07:55.827 --> 00:07:57.056
I don't mean in a bad way.
我不是在贬义上说这个。

00:07:57.056 --> 00:08:04.336
But I remember she would, if she would see you guys or any of the actor, any of the cast, go right to their phone and then be on the phone the whole time.
但我记得，如果她看到你们或者任何演员、任何卡司，直接拿起手机然后一直在玩手机。

00:08:04.336 --> 00:08:06.605
And we're coming up on her calling action again.
而我们马上又要听到她喊“开始”了。

00:08:06.605 --> 00:08:10.339
She would, while she would look over and she would just say, an actor prepares.
她就会一边看过来，然后冷不丁地说一句：“一个演员的自我修养。”

00:08:10.339 --> 00:08:13.390
You know, I did, it was devastating.
你知道的，我当时觉得这简直是毁灭性的打击。

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:18.220
It's all she had to say through words and actor prepares.
她只需要说这几个字：“一个演员的自我修养”。

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:29.660
I did a show for NBC for a season called Rise, which was a really lovely show that Jason And I gave myself a challenge that I stuck to the entire time, which was I never brought my phone to set.
我曾在NBC拍过一季名为《非凡up》的剧，那是一部非常温馨的剧，由杰森……我给自己设定了一个挑战，并且从头到尾都坚持了下来，那就是我从来不把手机带到片场。

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:36.820
I would have it in my dressing room, I would check it when I had to go do a costume change or whatever.
我会把它放在化妆间里，等我去换戏服或者干嘛的时候看一眼。

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:40.500
I never once brought it set, but it was also when I was learning guitar.
我从来没把它带到片场过，但那也是我刚开始学吉他的时候。

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:49.299
So I brought my guitar to set and we were often filming in this theater, this big auditorium that they actually built on a stage in Green Point in Brooklyn.
所以我把吉他带到了片场，我们当时经常在一个剧院拍戏，那是他们实际上在布鲁克林绿点的一个舞台上搭建的大礼堂。

00:08:49.299 --> 00:08:53.919
And I would sit in the audience and I would, you know, learn my lines, but I would noodle around on the guitar.
我就会坐在观众席里，你知道的，背台词，但同时也会拨弄几下吉他。

00:08:53.919 --> 00:09:03.220
