Like the things that make New York a small town are delightful.
让纽约变成一个小镇的那些事情真的非常有趣。

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.259
And I think that's what Tina is talking about.
我想这也是蒂娜在谈论的内容。

00:16:55.259 --> 00:16:56.740
And I think that's what Robin's job.
我想这也是罗宾的工作。

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.700
I know Tina was talking about in Jersey, but it's the same idea.
我知道蒂娜说的是在新泽西，但道理是一样的。

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.340
Like there's something about taking a big place and making it small.
把一个巨大的地方变得很小，这其中有种奇妙的感觉。

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:03.700
And Robin's job is so small.
罗宾的工作是那么卑微。

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:08.920
And her detail, she was on shit detail of just looking at the stupidest little story she wanted to be taken seriously.
她负责的都是那些琐碎的差事，只能盯着那些她希望被认真对待的最愚蠢的小新闻。

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:13.880
But I think because she was your way into this, like, smaller version of New York, it was actually very charming.
但我觉得，因为她是带你走进这个更小版本的纽约的引路人，所以实际上非常迷人。

00:17:14.279 --> 00:17:16.079
And that's a bit too much of a game in Akron.
这在阿克伦有点太像是个游戏了。

00:17:16.079 --> 00:17:19.119
To not be overwhelmed by New York, you have to make it smaller for your.
要想不被纽约压垮，你必须把它缩小到适合你的尺寸。

00:17:19.119 --> 00:17:20.528
It has to be small.
它必须是小的。

00:17:20.528 --> 00:17:21.028
Yeah.
对。

00:17:21.028 --> 00:17:21.528
Yeah.
对。

00:17:21.528 --> 00:17:22.028
Yeah.
对。

