节目里的这个小亮点，你觉得怎么样，“泰德化”？

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:46.559
I thought it was tedding Derry.
我以为是“泰德·德里”。

00:17:46.559 --> 00:17:52.119
It was tedding Derry, my son's phrase, that I'm heartbroken we didn't use.
是“泰德·德里”，我儿子的口头禅，我因为没用上而心碎。

00:17:53.319 --> 00:18:01.680
Yeah, I thought the fact that they loved Ted enough to have him as a verb and like different verb conjugation meaning, I think it felt very warm to me.
对，我觉得他们对泰德喜爱到把他当成一个动词来用，还有不同的动词变位和含义，这让我觉得非常温暖。

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:05.680
It felt like they loved Ted and Ted didn't seem to take it too hard.
感觉他们很爱泰德，而且泰德似乎也没有太放在心上。

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:11.759
And any jokes where this group shares history, I love it, where they know Ted's story verbatim.
任何展现这群人共同经历的笑话我都喜欢，他们对泰德的故事倒背如流。

00:18:11.759 --> 00:18:12.599
Yeah.
对。

00:18:12.599 --> 00:18:19.200
They do something that I think it's very affectionate and who better to take the piss out of you and give you shit than you're the people who love you the most.
他们做了一件我认为非常充满爱意的事，而且还有谁比那些最爱你的人更适合取笑你、挖苦你呢？

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:26.640
I also think there's something about being in a group of people, maybe friends, maybe just coworkers or whatever.
我也觉得，身处一群人之中，也许是朋友，也许只是同事什么的。

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:33.759
